1
00:00:00,335 --> 00:00:02,210
There was a lottery where buying tickets

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,260
made you money.

3
00:00:03,852 --> 00:00:04,502
In Michigan,

4
00:00:04,502 --> 00:00:06,339
a game called Winfall had a strange

5
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:07,127
rule.

6
00:00:07,127 --> 00:00:09,402
If the jackpot passed five million dollars

7
00:00:09,402 --> 00:00:10,477
and nobody won it,

8
00:00:10,477 --> 00:00:12,177
the money rolled down to the smaller

9
00:00:12,177 --> 00:00:13,152
prizes.

10
00:00:13,752 --> 00:00:14,352
Suddenly,

11
00:00:14,327 --> 00:00:16,177
matching just a few numbers paid far

12
00:00:16,177 --> 00:00:17,427
more than usual.

13
00:00:17,993 --> 00:00:20,430
A retired shopkeeper named Jerry Selbee did

14
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:21,768
the maths in minutes.

15
00:00:21,768 --> 00:00:22,718
On those weeks,

16
00:00:22,718 --> 00:00:24,355
the average ticket was worth more than

17
00:00:24,355 --> 00:00:25,243
it cost.

18
00:00:25,827 --> 00:00:27,227
So he bought thousands.

19
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:28,227
Over nine years,

20
00:00:28,227 --> 00:00:29,814
he and his wife Marge won almost

21
00:00:29,814 --> 00:00:32,377
twenty-seven million dollars in prizes.

22
00:00:32,985 --> 00:00:33,585
Legally.

23
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:34,760
They didn't cheat the lottery.

24
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,110
They read the rules.

25
00:00:36,727 --> 00:00:38,002
Every roll-down week,

26
00:00:38,002 --> 00:00:39,652
the maths said the same thing.

